WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.615
Rachel Kim: Alright, it’s 10:01, let’s get started. Hope everyone’s doing okay this morning.

2
00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:11.054
Diego Santos: Morning! I’m good, just fighting with my inbox as usual.

3
00:00:12.143 --> 00:00:17.528
Amara Nwosu: Hey all, I’m here. Sorry, my dog decided to bark right as I joined.

4
00:00:18.775 --> 00:00:23.775
Omar Haddad: No worries, Amara. I’m on my second coffee, so I’m ready for anything.

5
00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:31.164
Nadia Petrova: Hi everyone! I’m here too. It’s raining in Boston, so I’m jealous of anyone with sun.

6
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:38.253
Rachel Kim: Haha, it’s actually sunny here for once. Okay, quick round of updates—Diego, you want to start?

7
00:00:38.507 --> 00:00:46.199
Diego Santos: Sure. Marketo sync is back to normal after that hiccup on Tuesday. I’ll keep monitoring, but we should be good.

8
00:00:47.092 --> 00:00:54.784
Amara Nwosu: Lead scoring model is almost ready for the Q3 rollout. I’ll send the doc for review by end of day.

9
00:00:55.844 --> 00:01:02.382
Omar Haddad: Revenue numbers are trending up, so that’s a nice change. I’ll share the dashboard link after this.

10
00:01:02.672 --> 00:01:10.364
Nadia Petrova: Sales team is prepping for the August push. We might need more support on event follow-ups, just a heads up.

11
00:01:11.406 --> 00:01:19.483
Rachel Kim: Thanks, everyone. Let’s jump to the main item—Goldcast best practices. We’ve had a couple issues with the pre-event check-in timing, right?

12
00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:25.084
Diego Santos: Yeah, last week two speakers joined like, three minutes before start. It was stressful.

13
00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:32.369
Amara Nwosu: I noticed that too. We barely had time to test their mics. Ten minutes isn’t cutting it.

14
00:01:33.206 --> 00:01:37.821
Omar Haddad: I agree. From analytics, sessions with late check-ins had more tech issues.

15
00:01:38.585 --> 00:01:44.739
Nadia Petrova: Sales heard complaints from a couple speakers about feeling rushed. Maybe we need to be clearer?

16
00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:49.640
Rachel Kim: So, should we bump the required backstage time? What’s realistic—fifteen minutes?

17
00:01:50.999 --> 00:01:56.769
Diego Santos: Fifteen makes sense. Gives us a buffer if someone’s late or has a camera issue.

18
00:01:57.566 --> 00:02:03.720
Amara Nwosu: Yeah, and it matches what other teams do. I checked the webinar doc from last quarter.

19
00:02:04.119 --> 00:02:06.427
Omar Haddad: I’m for it. Less last-minute scrambling.

20
00:02:06.856 --> 00:02:12.240
Nadia Petrova: Agreed. And we can update the speaker email template too, so it’s super clear.

21
00:02:13.119 --> 00:02:20.426
Rachel Kim: Okay, so we’ll change the policy to require speakers to be backstage at least 15 minutes before session start.

22
00:02:21.472 --> 00:02:27.241
Diego Santos: I’ll update the handbook page after this call. Should I also ping the events team?

23
00:02:28.242 --> 00:02:33.626
Rachel Kim: Yes, please. And let’s make sure the next event invite reflects the new timing.

24
00:02:35.022 --> 00:02:40.791
Amara Nwosu: Should we add a note about why we’re changing it? Like, for smoother tech checks?

25
00:02:41.998 --> 00:02:46.614
Rachel Kim: Good idea. Diego, can you add a quick rationale to the page?

26
00:02:47.418 --> 00:02:51.264
Diego Santos: Will do. I’ll draft something and send it for review.

27
00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:55.230
Omar Haddad: Thanks, Diego. That should help with buy-in.

28
00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:01.969
Nadia Petrova: And I’ll update the sales enablement doc with the new timing, just so everyone’s aligned.

29
00:03:02.588 --> 00:03:06.050
Rachel Kim: Perfect. Anything else on Goldcast before we move on?

30
00:03:06.569 --> 00:03:08.877
Amara Nwosu: Nope, that covers it for me.

31
00:03:10.292 --> 00:03:11.792
Diego Santos: All good here.

32
00:03:12.354 --> 00:03:13.854
Omar Haddad: Same.

33
00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.140
Nadia Petrova: Good here.

34
00:03:17.316 --> 00:03:21.547
Rachel Kim: Alright, last agenda item—team offsite survey. Omar, you had an update?

35
00:03:22.488 --> 00:03:29.411
Omar Haddad: Yeah, so 80% of folks voted for September 19th for the offsite. I’ll confirm the venue this week.

36
00:03:30.479 --> 00:03:33.172
Amara Nwosu: Is that the one near the river?

37
00:03:33.809 --> 00:03:37.655
Omar Haddad: Yep, the Riverside Center. They have space and good WiFi.

38
00:03:38.498 --> 00:03:42.344
Diego Santos: Nice, I’m in. Do we need to RSVP or anything?

39
00:03:42.966 --> 00:03:46.812
Omar Haddad: I’ll send a calendar hold and RSVP link by tomorrow.

40
00:03:47.646 --> 00:03:49.954
Nadia Petrova: Thanks, Omar. Looking forward to it.

41
00:03:50.615 --> 00:03:54.077
Rachel Kim: Great, thanks for organizing. Anything else before we wrap?

42
00:03:54.613 --> 00:04:01.536
Amara Nwosu: Just a quick one—can someone resend the link to the new lead routing doc? I can’t find it.

43
00:04:02.099 --> 00:04:04.792
Diego Santos: I’ll drop it in Slack after this.

44
00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:14.613
Rachel Kim: Thanks, Diego. Okay, action items: Diego updates the Goldcast handbook, Omar sends the offsite RSVP, Nadia updates sales docs. Did I miss anything?

45
00:04:15.957 --> 00:04:17.495
Omar Haddad: That’s it from me.

46
00:04:18.418 --> 00:04:19.918
Nadia Petrova: All set.

47
00:04:20.789 --> 00:04:22.289
Amara Nwosu: Good here.

48
00:04:22.738 --> 00:04:24.276
Diego Santos: Yep, I’m on it.

49
00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:28.636
Rachel Kim: Awesome. Thanks, everyone. Have a good rest of your Thursday!

50
00:04:29.365 --> 00:04:30.865
Omar Haddad: You too!

51
00:04:31.786 --> 00:04:33.286
Nadia Petrova: Bye all!

52
00:04:33.799 --> 00:04:35.299
Amara Nwosu: Bye!

53
00:04:36.118 --> 00:04:37.618
Diego Santos: See ya!
